<% content_for :title, "Getting started · Admin panel · Inkwll" %>
<% wellkeeper = t("terms.staff_levels.wellkeeper") %>
<% scribe = t("terms.staff_levels.scribe") %>
<% page = t("terms.staff_levels.page") %>

<article class="guide guide--admin">
  <h1 class="page-title">Getting started for staff</h1>
  <p class="guide__intro text">
    What to set up first in a new game, in a sensible order, and where to find
    the everyday jobs. You only see the admin menu links your staff level
    allows, so some of these may be done by someone else.
    <%= link_to "The players' guide", getting_started_path %> explains the game from their side.
  </p>

  <section class="guide__section guide__section--setup">
    <h2 class="section-title">Setting up the game</h2>
    <ol class="guide__steps list">
      <li class="guide__step list__item">
        <strong class="emphasis"><%= link_to "Game settings", edit_admin_game_settings_path %>:</strong>
        give the game its name and a short blurb for the front page. Decide
        whether players need an email address, whether characters need
        approval, and the game's date. <span class="guide__who muted">(<%= wellkeeper.pluralize %>)</span>
      </li>
      <li class="guide__step list__item">
        <strong class="emphasis"><%= link_to "Look", edit_admin_skin_path %>:</strong>
        pick a ready-made look or set your own colours, fonts, pictures and
        extra CSS. <span class="guide__who muted">(<%= wellkeeper.pluralize %>)</span>
      </li>
      <li class="guide__step list__item">
        <strong class="emphasis"><%= link_to "Features", edit_admin_features_path %>:</strong>
        switch SOUL, Inklings, Grimoire, the wiki, guest chat and the compass
        on or off. <span class="guide__who muted">(<%= wellkeeper.pluralize %>)</span>
      </li>
      <li class="guide__step list__item">
        <strong class="emphasis"><%= link_to "Building", admin_areas_path %>:</strong>
        a new game comes with a starter map to rename or replace. Make
        <%= term(:area, count: 2).downcase %>, put <%= term(:room, count: 2).downcase %>
        in them and join those with <%= term(:exit, count: 2).downcase %>.
        "Build several" makes many at once. Tick "New characters start here" on
        one <%= term(:room).downcase %>, and "Default <%= term(:room).downcase %>"
        on the one each <%= term(:area).downcase %>'s Enter button leads to.
        <span class="guide__who muted">(<%= scribe.pluralize %>, and <%= page.pluralize %> with the Build job)</span>
      </li>
      <li class="guide__step list__item">
        <strong class="emphasis"><%= link_to "Profile fields", admin_profile_fields_path %> and
        <%= link_to "Character groups", admin_character_groups_path %>:</strong>
        the questions on a character's profile and application, and the groups
        characters belong to. <span class="guide__who muted">(<%= wellkeeper.pluralize %>)</span>
      </li>
      <li class="guide__step list__item">
        <strong class="emphasis"><%= link_to term(:forum_board, count: 2), admin_forum_boards_path %>:</strong>
        the news, advertising and wanted ads boards, and who can post on each.
        <span class="guide__who muted">(<%= scribe.pluralize %> and up)</span>
      </li>
      <li class="guide__step list__item">
        <strong class="emphasis"><%= link_to "Players and staff", admin_accounts_path %>:</strong>
        bring in your team once they've signed up. <%= page.pluralize %> do the
        jobs you give them (Build, App), <%= scribe.pluralize %> run the game
        day to day, <%= wellkeeper.pluralize %> can change everything, and only
        a <%= term(:founder) %> can make a <%= wellkeeper %>. You can also mark
        players as <%= term(:storyteller).pluralize %>.
        <span class="guide__who muted">(<%= scribe.pluralize %> and up)</span>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="guide__section guide__section--daily">
    <h2 class="section-title">Day to day</h2>
    <p class="text">
      <strong class="emphasis">Waiting on staff</strong> at the top of the admin
      menu shows a number when something needs you: character applications,
      roster requests, and SOUL or Inkling requests if those are on.
      <strong class="emphasis">Reports</strong> holds anything players have
      reported, where you can lock a <%= term(:scene).downcase %>, hide a
      <%= term(:pose).downcase %> or warn a player, and
      <strong class="emphasis">Bans</strong> keeps people out when you need to.
    </p>
    <p class="text">
      Staff see a hidden <%= term(:scene).downcase %> only once it has been reported.
    </p>
  </section>
</article>
